- Interest income
  - The $1,115 of bank/broker interest is taxable on Form 1040 (reported from 1099-INTs if issued).

What you generally cannot deduct
- Unreimbursed employee expenses for your W-2 job (for most taxpayers through 2025). If the $780 were personal/unreimbursed employee expenses, they are not deductible.
- Student loan interest paid in prior years (only interest paid in the tax year is deductible for that year).
- Charitable gifts if you don’t itemize (unless special one-year provisions exist — not for 2024).

Should you itemize or take the standard deduction?
