   - Use the actual home‑office method (Form 8829) rather than the simplified method — it looks more favorable with your rent unless other constraints apply.
   - Claim student loan interest up to $2,500 if you actually paid that amount in 2024 and your MAGI permits it — otherwise claim whatever portion you paid that year (per Form 1098‑E).
   - Take the standard deduction for MFJ for 2024 (likely ~$29,200) unless you have additional itemizable deductions that push your Schedule A total above that.

