Assumptions I’m using
- The $12,500 is self‑employment income (you had 3 web design clients) and the home office is used for that business.
- The $780 “unreimbursed expenses” are business expenses for the web design work. If they were unreimbursed employee expenses for your W‑2 job, those are not deductible for tax years after 2017.
- The $3,600 student‑loan interest: I need to confirm whether that $3,600 was paid during tax year 2024 (only interest paid in the tax year is deductible). If it was paid earlier years, it is not deductible on the 2024 return.
