- Form 1040
- Schedule 1 (additional income and adjustments) — student loan interest deduction and half SE tax go here
- Schedule C (Profit or Loss from Business) — report web design income and business expenses
- Schedule SE — calculate self‑employment tax
- Form 8829 — if you use the actual home office method (apportionment of rent/utilities, etc.)
- 1099‑INTs for interest income (Chase, Schwab)
- W‑2 from Metro Consulting
- 1098‑E from MOHELA if you paid student loan interest in 2024 (or loan statements showing payments)

State (Massachusetts)
- File MA Form 1 (Massachusetts Resident Income Tax Return). Report W‑2 wages, interest, and the net self‑employment income (Massachusetts generally starts from federal AGI and has its own modifications). State rules differ for deductions and credits — but you’ll still report the Schedule C net income on the MA return. If you want, I can list MA specifics (standard exemption amount, any adjustments) once you confirm you want state‑level detail.

