What you must report
- W‑2 wages on Form 1040 (attach/enter W‑2 info).
- Self‑employment income (web design) on Schedule C (Profit or Loss from Business). Report the $12,500 as gross receipts, and deduct business expenses on Schedule C (see below).
- Interest income ($1,115) on Form 1040 — include amounts from your 1099‑INTs. (You only need Schedule B if your taxable interest + ordinary dividends exceed $1,500; you’re under that threshold.)
