Which of your items are deductible and how
- Self‑employment business expenses ($780): If those $780 are expenses directly related to the web design business (software, hosting, supplies, advertising, phone/data prorated for business use, etc.), they are deductible on Schedule C and reduce your net business profit. If the $780 are unreimbursed employee expenses from your W‑2 job, those are NOT deductible for tax years 2018–2025 under current law (unless you have a special situation like reservist/qualified performing artist, etc.).
  - Action: Confirm whether the $780 are business expenses for the web design work. If yes — deduct on Schedule C.

- Home office: You can claim a home office deduction for the part of your home used exclusively and regularly for the web design business. You have two methods:
