  2. Actual expenses method: allocate a portion of your actual home expenses to the business based on square footage. Your allocation = 100 / 690 ≈ 14.493%. For rent only, that’s 14.493% × $28,800 = $4,176 for the year (plus you could allocate utility/insurance costs if you pay those and include them in the calculation). The actual method usually gives a larger deduction here because your rent is substantial.
