- Schedule C — profit or loss from business (web‑design income $12,500 and business expenses).  
- Schedule SE — self‑employment tax.  
- Form 8829 — Expenses for Business Use of Your Home (only if you use the actual expense method for the home office). If you use the simplified method you generally won’t file Form 8829.  
- Schedule A — only if you itemize (charitable gift $800 would go here). Likely you won’t file this if you take the standard deduction.  
- Schedule B — only required if total taxable interest/dividends > $1,500 or other special conditions (your interest total $1,115 is under that line).  
- Form 8995 or 8995‑A — to claim the QBI (20%) deduction if applicable (Form depends on your total taxable income and business type).  
- Keep Form 1099‑NEC / 1099‑MISC (if any clients issued them) and any Form W‑2 from Metro Consulting. If you got paid > $600 by clients, you may receive 1099s — but you must report the income even if you did not receive a 1099.

6) Practical next steps and recordkeeping
- Confirm whether the $780 is business‑related. If yes, list the expense types (supplies, software, mileage, etc.) and dates/receipts. If not business related, it’s probably non‑deductible (if for W‑2 job).  
