- If you’ll use the actual home‑office method, collect rent statements, utility bills, insurance, and any direct business expenses for the office. If you prefer simplicity and/or expect actual allocation to be small, you can use the simplified method. In your case, the actual method looks better because rent is high.  
- Keep receipts and documentation for the $800 charitable contribution (bank record/acknowledgment).  
- Consider estimated tax payments: since you have self‑employment income, you may need to make quarterly estimated tax payments for income and SE tax (Form 1040‑ES) or increase withholding on your W‑2 income to cover the expected tax.

7) Rough illustration (example scenario)
