- Estimated tax payments: because you have self‑employment income, you may need to make quarterly estimated tax payments (Form 1040‑ES) during the year to avoid underpayment penalties if you expect to owe more than $1,000 when filing.
- Qualified Business Income (QBI): you will likely qualify for the 20% QBI deduction on part of your Schedule C qualified business income (Form 8995). That can reduce taxable income further. It’s computed after Schedule C and can be limited in certain circumstances, but with the income numbers you gave you’re probably under the thresholds and eligible.

Which is better: standard deduction or itemize?
