- Student loan interest > $2,500 (federal limit) and subject to MAGI phaseouts.

Itemize vs. standard deduction
- Standard deduction for 2024 (married filing jointly): $29,200 (IRS inflation-adjusted amount for tax year 2024).
- Likely itemized deductions you listed: $800 charitable + maybe state and local taxes (SALT) and mortgage interest if any (you didn’t list SALT or mortgage interest). With only $800 in charitable contributions and no other large itemized deductions shown, the standard deduction ($29,200) will almost certainly be larger — so take the standard deduction.
