What you can (generally) deduct
- Self-employment (web design)
  - Report income on Schedule C (Form 1040). You can deduct ordinary and necessary business expenses on Schedule C (software, supplies, advertising, business travel, part of your internet if used for business, etc.).
  - If the $780 are business expenses (not employee unreimbursed expenses), include them on Schedule C.
  - You’ll owe self‑employment tax on net self‑employment earnings (Schedule SE). You may deduct one‑half of the self‑employment tax as an adjustment to income on Form 1040.
