  - If you use 100 sq ft exclusively and regularly for your web‑design business, you can claim a home‑office deduction.
  - Two methods:
    - Simplified method: $5.00 per sq ft for up to 300 sq ft. For 100 sq ft that’s $500. Enter directly on Schedule C (no Form 8829).
    - Actual (regular) method: proportionate share of actual home expenses (rent, utilities, renter’s insurance, repairs, etc.). For rent you pay $2,400/month = $28,800/year. Business percentage = 100 ÷ 690 ≈ 14.4927%. Rent portion deductible for home office ≈ $28,800 * 14.4927% ≈ $4,174 (plus any prorated utilities/insurance/repairs). If you use the actual method you must complete Form 8829 (Business Use of Your Home) and attach it to Schedule C.
