Other practical items and tax planning notes
- Keep documentation: receipts for the $800 charitable gift, invoices/receipts for business expenses (the $780 if business), utilities/rent receipts for home‑office allocation, and Form 1098‑E.  
- If the $780 is business expenses, list them on Schedule C; if they are unreimbursed employee expenses from your W‑2 job, they are not deductible (federal).  
- If you expect to have similar self‑employment income going forward, consider making estimated quarterly tax payments (Form 1040‑ES) because SE tax plus additional income tax may leave you with tax due at filing. Generally you should pay estimated tax if you expect to owe $1,000+ after withholdings.  
