1) How each income item is reported
- W‑2 from Metro Consulting ($79,400): reported as wages on Form 1040 (W‑2 information goes on the wage lines of Form 1040).
- Web design income ($12,500 from 3 clients): treated as self‑employment income. Report on Schedule C (Profit or Loss from Business). Net profit from Schedule C flows to Form 1040 and is subject to income tax and self‑employment (SE) tax.
  - If you received any 1099‑NEC or 1099‑MISC for that work, include them; even if you didn’t receive 1099s you still report the income.
