2) Self‑employment tax and related deductions
- Self‑employment tax (Social Security + Medicare) is computed on Schedule SE. You pay SE tax on ~92.35% of your net self‑employment income.
- You can deduct half of your SE tax as an adjustment to income on Schedule 1 (so it reduces your AGI).

3) Business expenses and “unreimbursed expenses”
- Unreimbursed employee expenses (for a W‑2 job) are NOT deductible for most employees for tax years through 2025 (suspended by the Tax Cuts and Jobs Act), unless you are in a specific excepted category (e.g., certain performing artists, reservists). So if the $780 is unreimbursed expenses from your W‑2 job, you likely cannot deduct them.
