7) Federal forms you’ll typically need
- Form 1040 (U.S. Individual Income Tax Return)
- Schedule 1 (Additional Income and Adjustments to Income) — for taxable interest, student loan interest adjustment, etc.
- Schedule C (Profit or Loss from Business) — for your web design income and business expenses (home office, $780, etc.)
- Schedule SE (Self‑Employment Tax) — to compute SE tax
- Form 8829 (Expenses for Business Use of Your Home) — if you use the actual method for home office (many preparers use it to compute actual home‑use portion)
- Schedule A (Itemized Deductions) — only if you choose to itemize (likely not needed here)
