Short summary / bottom line
- You will almost certainly be better off taking the standard deduction on your federal return (married filing jointly) rather than itemizing, given the items you listed.
- Your student-loan interest is an above-the-line deduction (adjusts AGI) but is capped at $2,500 (not the $3,600 you paid).
- You have self-employment income from the web design work. Report it on Schedule C; you can claim a home-office deduction (actual or simplified) against that business, and you’ll owe self-employment tax (Schedule SE). Half of the SE tax is deductible as an adjustment to income.
- If your “unreimbursed expenses” are business expenses for the web design work, they are deductible on Schedule C. If they are unreimbursed employee expenses for a W-2 job, they are not deductible (TCJA suspension through 2025).
