  - If these are business expenses for your web design clients (e.g., software, supplies, internet portion), deduct them on Schedule C.
  - If these are unreimbursed expenses related to your W-2 employment, they are not deductible on your federal return (suspended).
- Self-employment tax:
  - You must pay self-employment tax on net self-employment earnings (Schedule SE). Half of the SE tax is deductible as an adjustment on Schedule 1.
- Qualified Business Income (QBI) deduction:
  - You may be eligible for the 20% QBI deduction on qualified business income from Schedule C (Form 8995 or 8995-A). With relatively low taxable income and a small net Schedule C profit, you will likely be able to claim some or all of the 20% QBI deduction. This reduces taxable income (not AGI).

3) Itemize or take the standard deduction?
- Based on the items you listed (only $800 charitable, no mortgage interest listed, no big medical or property taxes mentioned), your likely itemized total will be far below the standard deduction for married filing jointly. So take the standard deduction.
