- If you prefer a simple approach, use the simplified home-office method ($500) — it’s simpler and requires no Form 8829. But from the numbers you provided the actual method likely gives a larger deduction; just make sure it doesn’t produce a business loss that’s restricted by other rules.
- Double-check the student-loan interest phaseout for MFJ in 2024 to be sure you qualify for the full $2,500.

